    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Creating or updating an owner whose email is at mailinator.com, tempmail.com or guerrillamail.com now returns 400. The full test suite passes: 14 tests, 0 failures, including the acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain`.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **`rest/validation/OwnerEmail.java`** (new): checks the email's domain against the blocklist. An absent email is still allowed, and the comparison ignores case.\n- **`rest/validation/InvalidEmailException.java`** (new): the error thrown for a blocked address, built the same way as `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1`**: `OwnerEmail.validate(...)` runs in both `addOwner` and `updateOwner`, straight after the postcode check.\n- **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`**: a new handler turns that error into a 400 response that names the `email` field and the rejected value, in the same format as the postcode and telephone errors.\n- **`openapi.yml`**: the email field's description now mentions the rule.\n- **`OwnerEmailTests`** (new): unit tests for allowed and blocked addresses, mixed case and subdomains.\n\n**A choice you may want to reverse:** I also block subdomains of the listed domains (e.g. `x@eu.mailinator.com`), since those are the same disposable service. Lookalike domains such as `notmailinator.com` or `mailinator.com.au` are still accepted. If you want only exact matches, it's a one-line change in `OwnerEmail`.",
